          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "Generation — The posterity."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "Righteousness — The fruit or reward of his righteousness, which is God's blessing upon his estate."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "Darkness — In the troubles and calamities of life. He - The upright man."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 5,
              "v_end": 5,
              "text": "Lendeth — Gives freely to some, and lends to others according to the variety of their conditions. Affairs - His domestick affairs. Discretion - Not getting his estate unjustly, nor casting it away prodigally, nor yet withholding it from such as need it."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "Moved — Though he may for a season be afflicted, yet he shall not be eternally destroyed."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 7,
              "v_end": 7,
              "text": "Evil tidings — At the report of approaching calamities."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "Dispersed — His goods, freely and liberally. Righteousness - His liberality, or the reward of it. Ever - What he gives is not lost, but indeed is the only part of his estate, which will abide with him to all eternity."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 112,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "The desire — Either of the misery of good men; or of his own constant prosperity. We are here exhorted to praise God, ver. 1-3. Particularly for his glory and greatness, ver. 4, 5 And for his grace and goodness, ver. 6-9."
            }
          ]
        },
